{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773593224,"nonce":"U3Q3RglsDHzgpOWiXBGCmRXu4dw=","title":"Merge base branch into agent worktree on resume","message":"On resume, the agent branch may be behind the base branch if other work was merged in the meantime. This causes the agent to work against stale code, leading to conflicts at review time.\n\nFix: before handing off to the agent on resume, merge the latest base branch into the agent worktree. If the merge has conflicts, abort and let the agent work from the current state — the pre-review rebase will catch divergence later.\n\nAlso applies to fresh starts via the existing pre-review rebase (already implemented in core/rebase.py).\n\nREQ-001, REQ-006","files":null}]}